igh Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359130"} "Pole Vault, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031064"} "Long Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031078"} "Triple Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359198"} "Shot Put, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359221"} "Discus Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359244"} "Hammer Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359267"} "Javelin Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359290"} "Heptathlon, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "63758"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "64434"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "65109"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "65767"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "66488"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "257630"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "302000"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000739"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2013903"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/102"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "10,000 metres, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "12 August 2016 — 11:10"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/909"} "Estádio Olímpico João Havelange, Engenho de Dentro, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/359065"} "37 from 24 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Final only."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Run as a final only, this was less of a race than a time trial for Ethiopian " [:a {:href "/athletes/130029"} "Almaz Ayana"] ". Kenyan " [:a {:href "/athletes/130889"} "Alice Aprot"] " took the early lead and held it through 5,000 metres, passed in 14:46.81, a PR for her for the shorter distance, but Ayana was right behind her in 14:47.1. They remained like that through 13 laps when Ayana decided to start her time trial, running the next lap in 66.5. Only " [:a {:href "/athletes/88160"} "Vivian Cheruiyot"] " was anywhere near her at the end of the lap."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Ayana continued, running metronomic laps to the finish, shattering the world record by running 29:17.45. The previous official world record was 29:31.78 by China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/66459"} "Wang Junxia"] " but that mark was considered almost certainly performance-aided, and most track stat freaks felt the true world best was the 29:53.80 set by " [:a {:href "/athletes/115206"} "Meselech Melkamu"] " in 2009. Thus, Ayana’s time was over 36 seconds faster than that mark. She ran the second 5K in 14:30.4, her last 3,000 in 8:47.5, and the final four laps in 4:41.5."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Behind Ayana, the top 13 runners were pulled to PRs and there were multiple national records set. Cheruiyot finished in 29:32.53, followed by Ethiopian " [:a {:href "/athletes/104973"} "Tirunesh Dibaba"] " in 29:42.56, with Aprot missing the podium with 29:53.51. The 2-4 finishers were thus also under what was considered the legitimate world record. American " [:a {:href "/athletes/126587"} "Molly Huddle"] " finished sixth in a national record 30:13.17, as did Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/131769"} "Sarah Lahti"] " in 12th with 31:28.43, Burundi’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/83383"} "Diane Nukuri-Johnson"] " in 13th with 31:28.69, and Greece’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/130444"} "Alexia Pappas"] " in 17th in 31:36.16."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Lane"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time (Automatic)"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "641"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/13002